{
  "spec_version": "peer-reconciliation-ref-v1.2",
  "description": "Conformance vectors for peer-reconciliation-ref-v1. Six invariants are separately recomputable: canonical_envelope, structural_validity, signature_validity, signature_binding, comparator_state, and supersedes_chain_integrity (v1.1, present only when `supersedes` is set). A verifier that treats any pair of present observations as AGREED without checking action_ref equality will silently pass disagreed-001. A verifier that defaults a missing half to AGREED will silently pass unresolved-001. A verifier that does not check what each co_signer's signed_fields actually covers will silently pass replay-001 (v1.2) as AGREED. v1.1 added three optional additive checks: supersedes_chain_integrity (correction pointers), requested_at (recommended non-suppression timestamp), as_of (informational per-observation time). v1.2 adds signature_binding and the mandatory co_signer.signed_fields field -- see 'v1.2' in the spec for why this one is not additive the way v1.1's fields were.",
  "comparator_rule": "AGREED requires both observed=true, both signatures valid, both signatures' signed_fields covering {party_id, action_ref, interaction_id}, and matching action_ref. DISAGREED requires the same three readiness conditions with differing action_ref. Anything else (missing observation, invalid signature, or a signature that does not bind action_ref/interaction_id/party_id) is UNRESOLVED -- never defaulted to AGREED or DISAGREED.",
